    "content": "## Test Completion Summary\n\nI have successfully tested all 21 items from the resume builder application checklist. Here are the results:\n\n### ✅ PASSED (16 items)\n- **FT-1**: Users can create new resumes with blank sections and edit immediately\n- **FT-2**: Users can choose and switch between Modern, Classic, and Minimal templates with content preserved\n- **FT-3**: Users can edit contact details, summary, experience, education, and skills (add/edit/remove)\n- **FT-4**: Users can reorder sections and toggle visibility; preview updates immediately\n- **FT-5**: Users can hide and show preview without losing content or template selection\n- **FT-6**: Users can duplicate resumes, rename them, and edit copies independently\n- **FT-7**: Multiple distinct resume variations can be created and managed in session\n- **FT-8**: Users can search resumes by title (case-insensitive) and clear search to restore all\n- **CS-10**: Date format is consistent across all displays (Month YYYY format)\n- **IX-12**: Changes to fields and templates appear in preview immediately\n- **IX-13**: Section reordering and visibility changes update preview immediately\n- **IX-14**: Resume edits are retained when navigating between editor areas\n- **CT-15**: Preview renders all visible sections with content and maintains readability\n- **CT-16**: Content is retained across tab navigation and dashboard returns\n- **CT-17**: Duplicated resumes are completely isolated; editing copy doesn't affect original\n- **CT-18**: Resume titles are consistently shown in editor header and dashboard\n- **CT-20**: Custom section headings are displayed correctly in preview\n\n### ❌ FAILED (5 items)\n- **FT-19**: Date range filtering UI not found/not implemented on dashboard\n- **CS-9**: Invalid date ranges (end date before start date) accepted without validation error\n- **CS-11**: Resume data not persisted after page reload - edits and new resumes are lost\n- **CS-21**: Empty/whitespace-only titles accepted without validation; blank resumes created\n\n### Key Findings\nThe application successfully handles most core resume building features including editing, templating, and session-based management. However, there are critical gaps in:\n1. **Data Persistence**: Changes are not saved after page reload\n2. **Input Validation**: Date ranges and resume titles lack validation\n3. **Advanced Filtering**: Date range filtering feature is not implemented\n\nThe application is functional for use within a single session but would benefit from implementing backend persistence and input validation before production use."
  }
}
